+          // Always advance the watchdog if we got a request and we're
+          // registered — even if PX4 has temporarily flipped our bit out of
+          // the valid_registrations_mask (because we were briefly flagged
+          // unresponsive). PX4 re-includes us once it sees fresh replies
+          // (externalChecks.cpp:246), so killing the node here on a
+          // recoverable hiccup just causes pointless re-registration churn
+          // and a multi-second window where arm triggers failsafe-Land.
+          _check_triggered = true;
+          if (!_first_request &&
